# API documentation

OpenAPI via swag godoc comments on handler methods. Generated output in `docs/`. Root router blank-imports `_ "<module>/docs"`.

## Required per endpoint

```go
// GetByID godoc
// @Summary      Get order by ID
// @Description  Returns a single order
// @Tags         Orders
// @Produce      json
// @Param        id   path      string  true  "Order ID"
// @Success      200  {object}  models.OrderResponse
// @Failure      400  {object}  models.ErrorResponse
// @Failure      404  {object}  models.ErrorResponse
// @Failure      500  {object}  models.ErrorResponse
// @Router       /v1/orders/{id} [get]
func (h *orderHandler) GetByID(c echo.Context) error {
```

| Annotation | Required |
|------------|----------|
| `@Summary` | Yes |
| `@Tags` | Yes — one tag per feature |
| `@Router` | Yes — path and method must match `config/.../router/` |
| `@Success` | Yes — use `models.*` types |
| `@Failure` | Yes for documented error responses |
| `@Param` | Yes for path, query, body inputs |
| `@Produce` / `@Accept` | When applicable |

## Main

```go
// @title       Acme API
// @version     1.0
// @description Order management API
// @BasePath    /
```

## Workflow

1. Add or change handler comments when routes or models change
2. Run `swag init` (or project makefile target)
3. Commit `docs/docs.go`, `swagger.json`, `swagger.yaml` if the repo tracks them

## Rules

- Types in `@Success` / `@Failure` must exist in `models/`
- Keep `@Router` in sync with feature router paths
- Update `AGENTS.md` endpoint list when routes change ([go-module-ai-doc.mdc](./go-module-ai-doc.mdc))

## Avoid

- Undocumented exported HTTP handlers
- Hand-editing generated `docs/docs.go`
- Mismatched tag names across endpoints of the same feature
